A||||6||FieroLisa||Sucks back and Surges on cold acceleration?||||13||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||08-23-2001||01:48 PM||||My car is unhappy. I'll keep it short, this is what happens.  The car is in a cool garage all night. I start it and it almost stalls till I gas it once, idle goes up to 1500 then holds steady at 1000 and I'm on my way to work.<BR>Then as I'm pulling out of the driveway, anytime I put my foot on the gas, however lightly she surges forward, sucks back real strong, and then will throw herself forward again. That'll happen 2 or 3 times in a row then I'm on my way to work and she runs great. It's not driver error or anything like that, it's a more recent thing (well several weeks recent)<BR>I KNOW I need a new muffler, I have a Spintech ordered and my car sounds like utter crap. Rattles from here back to Ohio anytime I put my foot on the gas pedal at anything lower than 2000 prm.<BR>Is this a muffler problem, I also hear a real loud hissing I'm not convinced is *just* from my cold air intake, so maybe a vacuum problem?<BR>Suggestions? Once running, she runs great except that rattle on acceleration. <P>Ahh one more thing, I was pulling out of the barn's long driveway, where we have to drive slowly, so I didn't my foot on the gas or brake, 1st gear, under 10mph and shes lightly surging back and forth, surging getting stronger as I go.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||13
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||02:07 PM||||Might be your MAP sensor or TPS.  Mine used to do that...violently.  The hissing is probably your IAC opening up a lot to compensate for driver error.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  hehe...or just because it thinks its going to stall.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>shes lightly surging back and forth, surging getting stronger as I go.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh, nevermind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Might want to check the service manual about "surging"... or "hunting" if it doesn't idle steady.<P>Joe<P><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||08-23-2001||02:09 PM||||I am having the same problem Lisa, and I have replaced all the ignition components, but the pick up coil.  I am going to change the pick up coil next.  After the car is warmed up for 20-30 minutes do you notce any misfiring when you are at a stop light?  Mine kind of makes the RPM gauge go from 800RPM to 1500 really fast, but it sounds like it is choking, not getting higher in RPM.  This is not much help, but at least from my experience with changing parts I know it is not any of the ignition componts, just possibly the pick up coil.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||3
Z||000003||lou_dias||08-23-2001||02:25 PM||||fuel pump...<P>chech your fuel pressure to be sure but i bet that's it.  my car did that once too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick86GT||08-23-2001||05:44 PM||||fuel pump pressure should be (i recall) 47# for the 2.8 to run....<P>recently, one of my 86's had weakened to 35# and wouldn't run the car for #$@&.  Right after replacing the pump, I got some codes: O2 sensor and ERG valve.  <P>May be a chain reaction...or just bad luck||||reg||1
Z||000005||Simple Fiero||08-23-2001||06:05 PM||||I am having the same problem you are Lisa. i hope someone figures this out cause it is starting to happen after I shift now too(so you have that to look forward too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. And about the fuel pump thing, I thought that might be it too so I replaced the fuel filter and then my pump died on me like a week afterwards. 450 dollars later and it still does the surging, I am going to replace the TPS next, and see what happens cause that isn't very expensive. Good luck on this.<P>Craig<P>88 SC<BR>4cyl||||reg||1
Z||000006||RAREW66||08-23-2001||06:19 PM||||Check those vacuum leaks. A cracked EGR tube on a V-6 will give the symptoms you describe.<P>Spray some carb cleaner around the tube and vacuum lines and where there is a leak, the idle of the engine will stumble slightly.<P>A worn out exhaust usually does nothing more than make the car sound bad. <P>P.S. I did'nt forget about the LP bracket, just been busy.We'll make a show car for ya somehow.<P>Fred||||reg||1
